{"user": "I think g2 makes more sense, it'll form one coplete straight line. After each legal move does white get a corner or strong edge?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T17:09:59.835907+00:00", "assistant": "Your instinct about **g2** making a line is understandable, but in endgames a line isn\u2019t safe unless it\u2019s **anchored by a corner**.\n\nAfter Black\u2019s legal moves:\n\n- **g2** \u2192 White can play **a1 corner**\n- **b6** \u2192 White can play **a1 corner** and has edge options\n- **a7** \u2192 White can play **a1 corner**\n- **b8** \u2192 White can play **a1 corner**\n- **c8** \u2192 White can play **a1 corner**\n- **b7** \u2192 White does **not** get a1, but can play **a8 corner**\n\nSo the question is: would you rather give White **a1**, or force a different corner trade after **b7**? Corners matter more than completing a temporary line.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T17:10:49.410806+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T17:10:51.443318+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Worked Line", "General Principle", "Prompt", "Paraphrase"], "consensus": ["Worked Line", "General Principle", "Prompt", "Paraphrase"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 3, "Paraphrase": 3, "Positive Feedback": 1, "Local Justification": 1, "Neutral Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Worked Line": 1.0, "Gen